<%--
Attachment_Thumbnail

THE way a thumbnail renders in an RSX app - images, PDFs, Office documents, everything. A caller
supplies an attachment id and a size; the component fetches the record, builds the URL, and keeps
the picture correct for as long as it is on screen.

It matters that this is a component and not a URL string in a payload: an Office document has no
thumbnail until the background render worker has produced its PDF rendition, so what the browser
first paints is an extension-icon placeholder. When the render lands, a realtime frame on the
attachment brings the component back for a fresh record and the picture swaps in place - no reload,
no polling, and no stale placeholder pinned by a one-year cache header.

Args:
  $attachment_id  (required) - the File_Attachment_Model id. Throws if absent.
  $type           (optional) - dynamic variant: 'fit' (default) or 'cover'.
  $width          (optional) - dynamic variant width in px (default 120).
  $height         (optional) - dynamic variant height in px; omitted -> width-only variant.
  $preset         (optional) - named preset from rsx.thumbnails.presets. MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE with
                               $type/$width/$height - passing both throws.
  $alt            (optional) - img alt text; defaults to the attachment's file name.

Extra classes go on the invocation as an ordinary HTML attribute - <Attachment_Thumbnail class="me-2"
$attachment_id=id /> - which jqhtml preserves on the host element; there is no $class arg.

States (data-render-status, on the rendered <img> or placeholder, carries the blob's
File_Storage_Model::RENDER_STATUS_*, or 'none' when there is no resident blob):
  1 NOT_REQUIRED - an image or PDF: the picture is rasterized straight from the blob.
  2 PENDING      - queued for render: the extension icon is served, uncacheable.
  3 RENDERED     - the real page-1 raster.
  4 FAILED       - terminal: the extension icon, permanently.
  unavailable    - the record could not be fetched (deleted, or not visible to this user).
--%>
<Define:Attachment_Thumbnail tag="div">
    <% if (!this.args.attachment_id) { throw new Error('Attachment_Thumbnail requires $attachment_id'); } %>
    <% if (this.args.preset && (this.args.type || this.args.width || this.args.height)) { throw new Error('Attachment_Thumbnail: $preset and $type/$width/$height are mutually exclusive'); } %>
    <%
        const _record = this.data.attachment;
        const _status = (_record && _record.file_storage) ? int(_record.file_storage.render_status_id) : 'none';
        const _alt = this.args.alt || (_record ? _record.file_name : '');
        const _src = _record ? File_Attachment_Model.thumbnail_url(_record, {
            type: this.args.type,
            width: this.args.width || 120,
            height: this.args.height,
            preset: this.args.preset,
        }) : null;
    %>
    <% if (_src) { %>
        <img class="Attachment_Thumbnail__img" src="<%= _src %>" alt="<%= _alt %>" data-render-status="<%= _status %>" data-attachment-id="<%= int(this.args.attachment_id) %>">
    <% } else { %>
        <%-- No record: deleted, or not visible to this user. A quiet empty box, never an error. --%>
        <div class="Attachment_Thumbnail__placeholder" data-render-status="unavailable" data-attachment-id="<%= int(this.args.attachment_id) %>"></div>
    <% } %>
</Define:Attachment_Thumbnail>
